From da0000a07512f912aafb8cdb4a9435eebd838b16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: amcheck <am@check>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 17:48:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] i686: share the constant-materialization model between
 both marshalling paths, and test it

The direct-store fold duplicated operand_to_eax's per-IrConst-arm value mapping
in a second match, and justified its zero exclusion from encoding sizes measured
at the point of emission. Both were latent defects:

* The duplication could drift. const_stack_arg_imm and const_zero_uses_xorl are
  now the single source of truth, used by operand_to_eax as well as by the fold,
  so the bytes a direct 'movl $imm, N(%esp)' stores are the bytes the register
  sequence would have stored by construction rather than by inspection.
* The emission-time cost model is the wrong one. Only I32/I64/Zero materialize
  zero with 'xorl' here, so a per-arm predicate looks like it should fold zeros
  in the I8/I16/I128/D32/D64/F32/F64/LongDouble arms ('movl $0,%eax' is 5B, the
  folded store 8B, so folding seems to win a byte). It loses two: the i686
  peephole normalizes 'movl $0,%reg' to 'xorl %reg,%reg' before the assembler
  sees it, so a zero costs 2B in every arm. Implementing the per-arm form and
  diffing emitted assembly per TU against the previous binary found 8 corpus TUs
  each growing 2 bytes; the blanket 'imm != 0' rule is restored, now justified
  by that mechanism instead of by a corpus census.

Tests: 6 unit tests over all eleven IrConst arms (bit-exactness, including -0.0f
as 0x80000000 and the F64 low-half truncation), the fold predicate re-derived
from byte-count constants at post-peephole cost for both displacement forms, and
no_zero_folds_in_any_arm as an explicit tripwire naming the peephole it depends
on. Plus tests/regression/i686_const_stack_args.c: 13- and 8-argument noinline
callees, every constant kind, zeros in every position, 8-byte arguments
interleaved to shift each following slot offset, the operands that must keep
using %eax (variable, alloca ADDRESS, global address, function pointer) and a
variadic call, checksummed by argument bit pattern against gcc -m32 references.
It passes at -O0/-O1/-O2/-O3 with the fold both on and gated off, and it fires
the fold 36 times against 29 gated, so it is not vacuous.

The refactor is output-neutral by measurement: 795/795 compilable corpus TUs emit
byte-identical assembly to the previous binary at -O0, -O1, -O2, -O3 and -Os.
