From: lccc-agent <agent@lccc.local>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 20:26:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] docs(i686): adjudicate the PR #512 audit finding by
 finding, with the measurements

Section 10 records what the audit got right, what it got wrong, and what was
done about each -- including the two places where the audit and this
implementation part company:

 * the fixpoint's monotonicity justification does not hold as merged (the
   state-restricted implicit-write probe is anti-monotone), so the fix makes
   the probe function-level rather than merely adding a second sweep;
 * F4's mechanism is wrong (%esp-biased slots are ours, ESP_SLOT_BIAS =
   1<<24) and its blanket remedy is rejected on measurement: 166
   instructions across 74 TUs, and it does not close the hole it was
   proposed for because a callee can write through the leaked pointer during
   a call, which that arm does not govern.

F2's severity is corrected upward (live today, not theoretical once loops
work) and F3's evidence is bounded honestly: a genuine violation of the
pass's own invariant, visible at 14 corpus sites and provable at the
assembly level, but not demonstrated as a wrong C answer, because making the
range overlap a live tracked slot takes aliasing only undefined behaviour
produces. Sections 3 and 9 are reconciled with the implementation, and the
two exec_diff behaviour deltas are adjudicated there rather than left as
noise: one benchmark is non-deterministic in every arm including base, and
one test's stated expectation is the LP64 answer to an i386 program.
